    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "Species for the query is not specified; if the target is rat, the FK788 rat F of 9.6% and S-propranolol rat F of 12% would be more concerning.",
    "No fed-state-specific bioavailability data are available for the exact aryloxyacetic acid fused-ring chemotype; the fed-state records are from a structurally unrelated peptidomimetic (KNI-272) and a basic beta-blocker (propranolol).",
    "Permeability, solubility, and active-transport status of the query are not experimentally established; the negative logD prior is physicochemical only.",
    "Dose and formulation effects on F for the query are unknown."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the most transferable L1 gold records—FK788 (55% human), etodolac (80-100% human), and fed KNI-272 (36.4%)—affirmatively support F >= 20%, and no L1 record provides affirmative evidence for F < 20%. New L2 records add some low species/formulation-specific values (FK788 rat 9.6%, KNI-272 fed syrup 15.7%, S-propranolol rat 12%) but these are not gold votes and do not overturn the human high evidence; the unfavorable logD prior is insufficient to override the empirical support."
}

